<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi all,I'm very new to dmr so don't shout at me.when open my local dmr repeater I can hear people but after a while it goes quiet until I open it again.is there a way of getting around this.<br>Regards</div></blockquote>Is it a Brandmeister repeater ?<br>If you key up a talkgroup it's normally active for 15 minutes and if there is no local activity the dynamic talkgroup is removed from the repeater.<br><br>Some repeaters have some static talkgroups. <br><br>Most DMR systems have some sort of portal where you can see such things.<br><br><a href="https://brandmeister.network/?page=repeaters" class="postlink">https://brandmeister.network/?page=repeaters</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sat Jun 07, 2025 8:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
